  "raw": {
    "https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com/postings/2173": {
      "title": "Lawrence University Portal | Assistant Women&#39;s Ice Hockey Coach",
      "description": "Lawrence University Portal | Assistant Women&#39;s Ice Hockey Coach Skip to Main Content Lawrence Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Women's Ice Hockey Coach Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Women's Ice Hockey Coach Location Appleton Department Athletics Position Type Staff Position Description & Qualifications Department: Athletics Reports To: Women’s Head Ice Hockey Coach and The Director of Athletics Job Status: Full-Time (12-month position) Classification: FT Exempt Job Summary: The Assistant Women’s Ice Hockey Coach will assist the Head Ice Hockey Coach with all duties of successfully operating our women’s ice hockey program, including but not limited to recruiting student-athletes, assisting with training sessions/game preparation/game-day coaching, monitoring the student-athletes academically, and managing game day operations. Lawrence University is a member of the NCAA Division III , Midwest Conference, Northern Collegiate Hockey Association, and Midwest Fencing Conference. Lawrence currently fields teams in 24 intercollegiate sports with approximately 400 scholar-athletes and is committed to a well-balanced program promoting excellence in both. When assisting the Head Women’s Ice Hockey Coach, any and/or all the duties listed below are the responsibility of the position: Plan and direct athletics skill development for student-athletes. Recruit student-athletes compatible with Lawrence University’s mission and the specific goals of the women’s ice hockey program. Assist in advising student-athletes and staff of applicable NCAA , NCHA , and ice hockey specific rules, regulations, and University policies and ensure compliance of such regulations. Assist the Head Coach in the review of practice and game video. Monitor student-athlete academic performance and implement team, Athletics department, and University measures to support their academic performance. Work with the University Athletic Trainers to ensure student-athletes receive proper medical and physical training services. Coordinate all activities in preparation for scheduled competition. Attend all team practices and home and away contests. Additional Responsibilities: Assist with game day management as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Successful collegiate coaching/playing experience. Ability to recruit qualified student- athletes. Bachelor’s degree required Master’s degree is preferred. Must have successful completion of criminal and MVR background check, meet University Authorized Driver Policy requirements, and favorable completion of reference checks. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S644P Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Date Best Consideration Date Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions Summary Anticipated Number of Hours per Week 40 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other If other, please specify (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Return To Lawrence Lawrence University 711 East Boldt Way Appleton, WI 54911 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com/postings/2176": {
      "title": "Lawrence Careers",
      "description": "Lawrence University Portal | Health Professions Career &amp; Experiential Learning Advisor Skip to Main Content Lawrence Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Health Professions Career & Experiential Learning Advisor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Health Professions Career & Experiential Learning Advisor Location Appleton Department Career Center Position Type Staff Position Description & Qualifications Location: Appleton Department: Career Center Position Type: Staff, Full-Time Job Summary The Health Professions Career and Experiential Learning Advisor is a full-time professional staff member in the Career Center, created as part of a five-year pilot initiative to strengthen support for students pursuing mental health and other health professions. Reporting to the Career Center Dean, the Advisor is an integral member of the Career Center team, providing individualized career advising alongside a specialized portfolio in internship development, career coaching, and postgraduate advising for pre-health and mental-health-interested students across Lawrence’s academic programs. The Health Professions Career Advisor and Experiential Learning Advisor builds and sustains relationships with local and regional healthcare organizations, mental health providers, and other internship hosts to expand students’ access to meaningful experiential learning opportunities. Through one-on-one coaching, workshops, and proactive outreach, the Advisor helps students develop the skills, professional networks, and confidence needed to pursue internships, employment, and graduate or professional study in health-related fields. This position reflects Lawrence University’s commitment to equitable access to career development. Students pursuing health professions often face distinct barriers — limited professional networks, lack of specialized career coaching, and financial constraints — and this role is designed to address them directly. Essential Job Responsibilities Experiential Learning Coordination Serve as the primary coordinator for health professions experiential learning, identifying, cultivating, and stewarding partnerships with local and regional healthcare organizations, mental health providers, clinics, and other internship hosts to expand internship capacity across pre-health fields. Develop and oversee internships and practicums for students interested in mental health and allied health careers, managing the full lifecycle from partner agreement through student application and placement, supervision check-ins, and post-internship/practicum evaluation. Build and maintain a structured pipeline of internship and experiential learning opportunities, including tracking host capacity, renewal timelines, and site-specific requirements. Connect students with alumni mentors and professionals in healthcare and related fields; organize networking events and industry-insight programming. Help coordinate financial support for students in unpaid or underpaid health-related internships, including funding for professional attire, transportation, and relocation, in accordance with program budget guidelines. Pre-Health Advising and Coordination Provide specialized one-on-one career advising to pre-health and mental-health-interested students, including resume and interview preparation tailored to clinical and health-related settings, workplace culture education, and networking guidance. Advise students on the postgraduate application process for pre-health and mental health graduate and professional programs, including timelines, required experiences, and personal statement development. Design and lead career workshops specific to healthcare and mental health professions, including programming in Lawrence’s Pre-Health Commons. Partner with academic departments (e.g., Psychology, Biology), pre-health advising committee, and campus offices supporting pre-health students to coordinate pre-health advising services and avoid duplication of services. As institutional needs evolve, this position may assume additional coordination or leadership responsibilities related to pre-health advising. Coordinate and maintain Career Center-managed web content and student-facing information related to health professions for prospective students, current students, and alumni, in partnership with the pre-health advising committee. Maintain accurate advising records and participate in Career Center-wide outcomes reporting, assessment, and staff meetings. Assessment and Campus Collaboration Track and report on student/alumni outcomes, including internship participation, skill development, job placement, and graduate/professional school acceptance; gather feedback from students and employer partners to continuously improve the program. Represent the Career Center at university events and campus partner meetings as assigned. Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrated coaching, advising, and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to build trusting relationships that promote student growth and confidence. Demonstrated ability to build and maintain external partnerships with employers, healthcare organizations, or community partners. Knowledge of career development theory, appreciative advising, or related developmental coaching approaches. Familiarity with pre-health/pre-graduate advising processes, application timelines, and admissions requirements a plus. Strong presentation, workshop facilitation, and one-on-one advising skills. Excellent organizational skills and ability to manage a caseload of students alongside employer and partner relationship management. Experience and demonstrated commitment to culturally responsive practice and working effectively with diverse student populations, including but not limited to first-generation students, international students, students with disabilities, LGBTQIA+ students, AAPI and BIPOC students, and students from a variety of cultural, religious, and socioeconomic backgrounds. Commitment to equitable access to career development resources for students facing financial or professional-network barriers. Demonstrated professionalism and ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment. Familiarity with, or the ability to quickly learn, student success and career technologies such as Handshake/Symplicity, Navigate360, Microsoft Outlook, Microsoft Excel, Microsoft Teams, and related platforms. Appreciation for the value of a liberal arts education and Lawrence University’s commitment to intellectual curiosity, creativity, exploration, and student development. Education and Work Experience Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. At least one year of experience in career advising, counseling, coaching, healthcare workforce development, or related student-facing higher education work. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in higher education, counseling, health administration, or related field. Three to five years of experience in higher education, preferably in career advising, health professions advising, or related direct student support roles. Experience building and maintaining employer or healthcare partnerships. Experience advising students on pre-health or pre-graduate program applications. Commitment to Equity, Inclusion, and Belonging Lawrence University is committed to fostering an inclusive campus where all students can thrive. We encourage applications from individuals who will contribute to this mission through their experiences, perspectives, and demonstrated commitment to supporting student success across diverse populations. Candidates should be prepared to discuss how their experiences and practices contribute to creating equitable and inclusive environments that support student learning, belonging, persistence, and achievement. Application Materials Please submit: Cover Letter Resume Posting Detail Information Posting Number S645P Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Date Best Consideration Date Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions Summary Anticipated Number of Hours per Week 40 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other If other, please specify (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Return To Lawrence Lawrence University 711 East Boldt Way Appleton, WI 54911 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com/postings/2102": {
      "title": "Lawrence Careers",
      "description": "Lawrence University Portal | Custodian Skip to Main Content Lawrence Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Custodian Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Custodian Location Appleton Department Campus Services - Custodial Position Type Staff Position Description & Qualifications Reports to : Assistant Director of Campus Services – Custodial Department : Campus Services – Custodial Location : Appleton, WI – Campus Buildings and Areas (as assigned) Hours : 5:00 am – 1:30 pm, Monday – Friday OR 6:00 am – 2:30 pm, Monday – Friday Position Summary The Custodian position provides a high level of customer service to all members of the campus community by performing a variety of custodial tasks and duties. Key responsibilities include basic cleaning, maintaining clean and orderly appearance inside of buildings, trash removal, and snow and ice removal. This position interacts frequently with staff, students, and faculty across the university environment. This position is 40 hours per week, Monday through Friday, with flexible shift times. Job Responsibilities and Accountabilities ( for your assigned area ) Clean and maintain all hard floor surfaces. Vacuum and spot clean all carpeted surfaces. Clean restrooms, showers and locker rooms and replenish dispensers (paper, soap, etc.). Clean all interior surfaces and areas in campus buildings. Remove and properly dispose of trash and recyclables in outside dumpster containers. Remove snow and ice from outside walkways and entryways. Make minor repairs as needed (replacement of light bulbs, etc.) Assist with special projects on an as-needed basis (summer and end-of-term cleanup, etc.) Knowledge and Skills Required Must be able to climb a 12 ft. stepladder. Must be able to lift 50 lbs. Ability to learn to use equipment i.e. mall hand tools, vacuums, etc. Must be able to read and follow instructions, directions, and safety procedures. Education and Work Experience High school diploma or equivalent preferred, but not necessary. Previous custodial/janitorial experience preferred, but not necessary. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S614P Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Date Best Consideration Date Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions Summary Anticipated Number of Hours per Week 40 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other If other, please specify (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Return To Lawrence Lawrence University 711 East Boldt Way Appleton, WI 54911 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
