    "https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com/postings/2174": {
      "title": "Lawrence University Portal | Assistant Professor, Data Science and Statistics",
      "description": "Lawrence University Portal | Assistant Professor, Data Science and Statistics Skip to Main Content Lawrence Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor, Data Science and Statistics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor, Data Science and Statistics Location Appleton Department Mathematics & Computer Science Position Type Faculty Position Description & Qualifications Lawrence University of Wisconsin, a selective undergraduate liberal arts college and conservatory of music located in Appleton, Wisconsin invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Data Science and Statistics to begin September 1, 2027. We seek candidates who will contribute to our growing program, which includes a new Data Science and Statistics major. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in statistics, biostatistics, data science, or a closely related field prior to the time of appointment (9/1/2027); ABD is acceptable for selection. Candidates should demonstrate potential for teaching a variety of undergraduate statistics and data science courses, and expect to participate in Lawrence’s flagship First Year Studies program on rotation. The First Year Studies curriculum presents an interdisciplinary introduction to the liberal arts intended to support new students’ fundamental skills as readers, writers, and thinkers. Primary duties include: teaching two undergraduate courses in each of Lawrence’s three ten-week terms, grading, advising and mentoring students; conducting research; leading occasional tutorials, supervising independent study projects and internships; assisting in curricular planning; and related departmental and institutional service. The successful candidate will be the third statistics and data science faculty member in the Department of Mathematics, Statistics, and Computer Science. Additional information about our curriculum and faculty can be found at https://www.lawrence.edu/academics/college/data-science-and-statistics . Candidates should submit the following: (1) a cover letter describing their interest in this position, (2) a curriculum vitae, (3) a statement of teaching explaining their pedagogical methods and teaching experiences, (4) a statement describing their scholarly activities, interests, and future plans, (5) names and email addresses for three references who can be contacted for letters of recommendation at a later stage in the process (at least one of whom can attest specifically to teaching). In their teaching statement, candidates are encouraged to discuss their experiences and ideas for teaching courses involving data analysis and computational tools. Candidates should also discuss how they will foster an inclusive and supportive learning environment for all students. In their scholarship statement, candidates are encouraged to discuss their experiences or ideas for incorporating undergraduate students in their research. Candidates are encouraged to read more about Lawrence at https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com as well as www.lawrence.edu and Colleges That Change Lives . We will begin reviewing applications on October 2, 2026. For further information, please contact Andrew Sage, the chair of the search committee ( sagea@lawrence.edu ). Posting Detail Information Posting Number S642P Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Date Best Consideration Date Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions Summary Anticipated Number of Hours per Week 40 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other If other, please specify (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Graduate School Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Statement on Teaching List of References Statement on Scholarship Optional Documents Return To Lawrence Lawrence University 711 East Boldt Way Appleton, WI 54911 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com/postings/2179": {
      "title": "Lawrence University Portal | Student Employment and Payroll Coordinator",
      "description": "Lawrence University Portal | Student Employment and Payroll Coordinator Skip to Main Content Lawrence Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Student Employment and Payroll Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Student Employment and Payroll Coordinator Location Appleton Department Human Resources Position Type Staff Position Description & Qualifications Reports to: AVP -Human Resources Location: 1025 Administrative Building The Student Employment and Payroll Coordinator is a full-time position that will be responsible for the day-to-day payroll operations of university student employment. This position’s principal role is to serve as the primary expert on the student employment lifecycle, from onboarding through employment changes, payroll, compliance, and offboarding of our domestic and international student workforce. This role serves as a central resource for student employment by understanding workforce needs, guiding payroll processes, and ensuring compliance with institutional and regulatory requirements. In addition, this position performs key administrative functions such as maintaining records, coordinating processes, communicating policies, and serving as the primary point of contact to support a consistent, high-quality experience for both hiring managers and student employees. The Student Employment and Payroll Coordinator provides frontline operational support to student employees, student supervisors, and campus partners, responds to inquiries, assists with navigating student employment and payroll processes, and resolves routine issues and escalates more complex issues to the appropriate authority. RESPONSIBILITIES AND DUTIES : Student employment Coordinate all aspects of student employment lifecycle. This includes collaborating with student supervisors on student job requests, developing and providing necessary communications, presenting at meetings, and serving as a point of contact for both students and student supervisors. Serve as a primary point of contact for student employees, student supervisors, and campus partners regarding student employment and payroll-related questions; provides guidance, resolve routine issues, and escalate complex matters as appropriate. Helps ensure a smooth and positive experience for both student managers and student employees by fostering effective collaboration, clear communication, and timely follow-up. Develop and maintains payroll specific reports, databases, and/or records to support accurate reporting, and compliance with established policies, procedures, and legal requirements and regulations. Audit and track required student employment and payroll activities, including onboarding, offboarding, background checks, employment eligibility, and other required steps, to ensure completion, accuracy, and compliance with university policies and applicable regulations. Maintain accurate and up-to-date student employment records and understand the varying requirements associated with student positions across university departments. Enter, review, and process a high volume of student employment hiring, job changes, and other HR actions in the system, ensuring accuracy and compliance with university policies and employment rules. Guide students and student supervisors through the employment onboarding process, helping ensure required employment documentation and procedures are completed accurately and within established timelines. Coordinate student employment/work study reporting requirements. Maintain necessary documentation for payroll records such as tax withholdings and direct deposits. Assist with the processing of W2s and 1042-S year-end filing as needed. Ensure accuracy and adherence to all payroll policies and procedures. Communicate student employment, payroll, and procedural requirements to students, student supervisors, and campus partners, including providing training or presentations when needed. International Student Employee Compliance Verify and track work eligibility for F-1 and J-1 students, ensuring they do not exceed work hour limits during academic terms. Support international students in obtaining Social Security Numbers ( SSN ) by providing the necessary employment verification letters. Work with the Payroll Manager to identify students eligible for tax treaties and ensure correct tax withholding (Tax Navigator, GLACIER or similar software management). Maintain a rigorous tracking system for expiring I-9 Forms, I-20s, DS-2019, Passports, and Visas to ensure continuous work authorization. Audit and monitor international student employment records and required documentation to identify upcoming expirations or compliance issues and coordinate appropriate follow-up. Communicate employment eligibility requirements and procedural information to international students and student supervisors as needed. KNOWLEDGE , SKILLS , AND ABILITIES REQUIRED : Proficient computer skills including MS Word, Excel, and Power Point. Prior experience with an HRIS database is strongly preferred. Exceptional organizational, prioritization, problem solving, attention to detail and follow-up skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality of sensitive information. Strong customer service skills, with demonstrated ability to work effectively with various groups and individuals. Experience working in a fast-paced, collaborative, and team-oriented environment with quickly shifting priorities Possess the ability to adapt and respond appropriately in ambiguous situations. Commitment to multicultural competency and interest in all dimensions of diversity. Collaborative attitude with team-oriented disposition with the ability to work independently. Strong ability to manage multiple competing priorities while demonstrating ability to remain flexible in a changing work environment. Strong interpersonal skills with a demonstrated ability to effectively and professionally communicate verbally and in writing with internal and external customers. Demonstrated initiative and ability to provide responsive, professional support to a diverse group of students, student supervisors, and campus partners. Ability to exercise sound judgment when addressing questions or issues and appropriately escalate matters requiring additional expertise or authority. EDUCATION AND WORK EXPERIENCE : High School diploma required. Associate degree preferred. One year of payroll experience preferred. Knowledge in federal and state payroll regulations preferred. EMPLOYMENT REQUIREMENTS : Must have successful completion of criminal record check, driving record check, and reference checks. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S646P Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Date Best Consideration Date Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions Summary Anticipated Number of Hours per Week 40 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other If other, please specify (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Return To Lawrence Lawrence University 711 East Boldt Way Appleton, WI 54911 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com/postings/2121": {
      "title": "Lawrence Careers",
      "description": "Lawrence University Portal | Financial Aid Counselor Skip to Main Content Lawrence Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Financial Aid Counselor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Financial Aid Counselor Location Appleton Department Financial Aid Position Type Staff Position Description & Qualifications Reports to: Director of Financial Aid Location: Lawrence University Appleton, WI PRIMARY OBJECTIVE The Lawrence University Financial Aid Office is a dedicated, student-centered team committed to delivering exceptional service while thoughtfully stewarding institutional, federal, and private financial aid resources. We strive to ensure that financial aid is administered equitably, transparently, and in alignment with the university’s mission and commitments to access and affordability. We are seeking an in-person Financial Aid Counselor to support this work. This role partners closely with students and families to navigate all aspects of the financial aid process—including application review, aid processing, and day-to-day office operations, while contributing to a responsive and service-oriented team environment. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Provide exceptional customer service. Serve as a designated point of contact for student needs regarding financial aid. Advise students and their families on all aspects of financial aid, including eligibility, application procedures, costs, processes, resources, etc. Review financial aid applications to determine financial need based on federal and institutional methodologies. Evaluation of financial aid eligibility includes verification of application requirements, reviewing and processing special circumstance requests, and documentation. Package financial aid in accordance with federal, state, and institutional policy. Perform data import to the Student Information System (Banner). Perform key processing functions that pertains to student documents and other financial aid requirements. Maintain current knowledge of federal and state financial aid programs, software, and regulations. Assist in the evaluation and implementation of department policies and procedures. Represent Lawrence University at financial aid conferences, trainings, workshops and meetings as agreed upon with the director. Perform other duties as assigned. WORKING RELATIONSHIPS This position will work collaboratively with other offices, specifically: Admissions, Student Accounts, and the Registrar’s Office; and other members of the Lawrence community. Additionally, opportunities to network with colleagues from other colleges and other members of the financial aid community are supported and expected. Work requires problem solving and decision-making guided by established policies, practices, and procedures. PREFERRED SKILLS AND KNOWLEDGE Commitment to customer service, including ability to maintain a positive attitude and professionalism. Ability to effectively and professionally communicate orally and in writing with diverse populations. Demonstrated digital literacy and technical expertise. Ability to recognize, analyze, and solve problems. Ability to organize workflow and handle multiple tasks simultaneously. Ability to maintain confidentiality of information with strong integrity and ethics. Demonstrated commitment, empathy, and sensitivity to meeting the needs of diverse populations. Excellent collaboration skills coupled with the ability to work both autonomously and as part of a team. REQUIRED MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS 1. Bachelor’s degree required. 2. Prior financial aid, admissions, or experience in higher education is preferred . Posting Detail Information Posting Number S622P Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Date Best Consideration Date Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions Summary Anticipated Number of Hours per Week 40 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other If other, please specify (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Return To Lawrence Lawrence University 711 East Boldt Way Appleton, WI 54911 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com/postings/2141": {
      "title": "Lawrence Careers",
      "description": "Lawrence University Portal | Dean of Students Skip to Main Content Lawrence Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Dean of Students Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Dean of Students Location Appleton Department Dean of Students Position Type Staff Position Description & Qualifications Lawrence University seeks a new Dean of Students ( DOS ) to prioritize the undergraduate and student experience while contributing on a variety of strategic and operational initiatives. Reporting to the Vice President for Student Life, the Dean of Students is an organizational manager, responsible for leadership of key Student Life units while fostering an inclusive environment. The DOS promotes and exemplifies Lawrence’s shared values – Belonging, Integrity, Respect, and Sustainability which are the foundation of the University’s culture, and which guide and inform the university’s strategic framework to empower the student population. The DOS is highly influential in creating a student and staff culture of inclusion, belonging, and innovation. Duties: Develop key collaborative and effective partnerships with campus administrative areas, faculty, and campus and community leaders to enhance planning and implementing strategic initiatives, resolving issues, in support of the student experience. Serve as a member of campus committees including CARE team, Crisis Management Team, Behavioral Intervention Team, Bias Response committee. Serve as the advisor to the Lawrence University Community Council (student government). Oversee, participate in, and direct the Student Life Administrators-On-Call system. Serve as the chief conduct officer of the university, overseeing all aspects of the student grievance process as well as the selection, training and advising of the Judicial Board. Provide leadership and guidance in annual analysis, review, creation and interpretation of student policies and procedures which are outlined in the University’s Student Handbook. Develop and execute strategies for integrated student engagement and learning in collaboration with Academic affairs. Oversight of the implementation of the First Year Dinner and Honors Reception. Provide leadership and oversight of Senior Committee activities, including Senior Week and Senior Banquet. Communicate effectively with students and other stakeholders. Work closely with campus partners to foster an inclusive campus community and promote equity of experience for all students. Supervise the offices of the SEAL / CCE Office, Residential Education, and the First Year Dean. Represent the Student Life Division to internal and external constituencies, including parents, community partners and professional associations. Other duties as assigned in performance of this student-focused student service position. Qualifications: Candidates should possess a master’s degree in higher education or a related field, as well as a minimum of 7 years of higher education experience in the area of Student Life with progressively increased responsibilities. A record of success as a supervisor, including but not limited to performance evaluations, professional development, setting individual goals, and assessment of performance effectiveness. Demonstrated professional effectiveness with broad experience interacting with and supporting the needs of a diverse student population. A high level of collegiality in working with other student affairs units as well as campus and community constituencies along with the ability to build collaborative relationships characterized by mutual respect, trust, and commitment to shared goals consistent with Lawrence’s stated mission. Integrity, creativity, energy, and decisiveness along with the capacity to engage and inspire others. Highly effective in all aspects of crisis management, including the ability to work collaboratively with others in managing crises. Experience in setting priorities and deadlines to ensure strategic planning goals and objectives are met. Strong skills in developing and managing budgets. Nuanced understanding of diversity, equity, and inclusion and antiracism including thoughtful ideas about how to meet the needs of Lawrence’s diverse student population. Interested candidates are asked to submit a current CV, letter of interest and three professional references. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S630P Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Date 07/09/2026 Best Consideration Date Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Anticipated Number of Hours per Week 40 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other If other, please specify (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation #1 Curriculum Vitae Letter of Reccommendation #2 Letter of Recommendation #3 Return To Lawrence Lawrence University 711 East Boldt Way Appleton, WI 54911 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com/postings/2146": {
      "title": "Lawrence University Portal | Visiting Assistant Professor of Theatre in Lighting and Sound",
      "description": "Lawrence University Portal | Visiting Assistant Professor of Theatre in Lighting and Sound Skip to Main Content Lawrence Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Visiting Assistant Professor of Theatre in Lighting and Sound Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Visiting Assistant Professor of Theatre in Lighting and Sound Location Appleton Department Theatre Arts Position Type Faculty Position Description & Qualifications The Department of Theatre Arts at Lawrence University invites applications for a full-time Visiting Assistant Professor of Theatre in Lighting and Sound to begin in the fall of 2026. Qualifications: Applicants should have a relevant MFA or relevant MA with college-level teaching experience Position responsibilities include: Teaching – 1 course per term: Production systems (lighting and sound) – annual Production Design – annual Sound and lighting design – biennial Advanced Design Studio, or develop a new course – biennial Lighting or Lighting and sound designs each term, for a total of 3 per academic year (in support of Theatre Arts Mainstage Productions and the Conservatory Opera) Ancillary responsibilities: Coordinate pre-production and on-site activities for 1-3 guest designers each year Guide sound and lighting lab students/student employees in conjunction with Production Manager (approx. 12 hours per week) Attend weekly production meetings and mentor student designers On-site supervisor (with Production Manager) for all tech rehearsals and performances Manage production budgets in area of responsibility Posting Detail Information Posting Number S632P Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Date Best Consideration Date Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions Summary Anticipated Number of Hours per Week 40 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other If other, please specify (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Return To Lawrence Lawrence University 711 East Boldt Way Appleton, WI 54911 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com/postings/2162": {
      "title": "Lawrence Careers",
      "description": "Lawrence University Portal | Student Success Coach Skip to Main Content Lawrence Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Student Success Coach Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Student Success Coach Location Appleton Department Center for Academic Success Position Type Staff Position Description & Qualifications Position Title: Student Success Coach Location: Appleton Department: Center for Academic Success Position Type: Staff Job Summary The Student Success Coach is a full-time professional staff member in the Center for Academic Success ( CAS ) and an integral member of Lawrence’s integrated student success hub. The Student Success Coach plays a central role in advancing Lawrence’s commitment to holistic student success by partnering with students to navigate the interconnected dimensions of academic achievement, personal growth, major and career exploration, career readiness, and purposeful decision-making throughout their Lawrence experience. The Student Success Coach provides individualized coaching, course instruction, workshop facilitation, outreach, and case management designed to help students succeed in their academic experience while developing the skills, habits, relationships, professional competencies, and sense of purpose necessary to thrive at Lawrence and beyond. Grounded in academic coaching principles, learning science, and a working knowledge of the Life Design framework, the Student Success Coach partners with students to intentionally design and navigate their college experience. Through coaching conversations and developmental interventions, the coach helps students build self-awareness, strengthen learning strategies, engage meaningfully with faculty and campus resources, explore possibilities, connect their academic experiences to personal values and future aspirations, and design and pursue intentional actions that lead to growth, achievement, and future success. Working in partnership with the Career Center and other campus partners, the Student Success Coach helps students connect their liberal arts education to meaningful careers and lives of purpose. The work of the Student Success Coach reflects Lawrence University’s commitment to supporting the whole student by recognizing that academic achievement, personal development, well-being, career readiness, belonging, and future direction are deeply interconnected. Essential Job Responsibilities: Student Coaching Provide individualized student success coaching that empowers students to identify their strengths, values, interests, and aspirations; clarify goals and priorities; make intentional decisions and take meaningful action; develop effective learning strategies; strengthen motivation, confidence, and accountability; and build resilience and self-awareness; and connect their academic experiences to meaningful engagement opportunities and future pathways. Partner with students to intentionally navigate their Lawrence experience by integrating academic success, personal growth, well-being, career readiness, and post-graduate planning into a cohesive educational journey. Guide students in exploring multiple academic, career, and life pathways through a developmental coaching approach emphasizing curiosity, experimentation, reflection, and iterative decision-making. Support students in developing effective college success behaviors, including faculty engagement, strategic help-seeking, time management, self-advocacy, reflective practice, and effective use of campus resources. Provide proactive outreach, coaching, and developmental support for students experiencing academic difficulty, navigating transitions, or encountering barriers to persistence and success. Coach students through the exploration of career pathways, graduate/professional education, and post-graduate opportunities using guided reflection, life design activities, informational interview planning, and intentional referrals to Career Center programs, alumni, employers, and experiential learning opportunities. Help students intentionally connect their liberal arts education to meaningful careers and lives by encouraging engagement in internships, undergraduate research, community-based learning, leadership, employment, global experiences, and other high-impact educational practices. Teaching and Facilitation Teach student success courses, such as: UNIC 153: Designing Your Life After Lawrence, a 3-unit course that applies design thinking principles to help students connect their Lawrence education with meaningful lives, careers, and multiple possible futures. Students engage in career exploration activities such as career narrative-building, informational interviewing, and prototyping possible career paths. UNIC 117: Academic Well-Being, a 3-unit course designed to introduce students to evidence-based well-being, learning, and academic success theories. Design and facilitate workshops and group learning experiences that integrate academic success strategies, career readiness, life design, and student development. Collaboration and Student Success Initiatives Collaborate with faculty, academic advisors, Career Center staff, and other campus partners to provide coordinated student support and ensure students experience seamless connections to campus resources and opportunities. Co-facilitate workshops and events focused on academic exploration, career development, alumni engagement, and experiential learning to help students build clarity, connections, and purposeful plans for their future. Serve as a connector within Lawrence’s student success ecosystem by helping students access academic support, career development resources, experiential learning, faculty mentorship, alumni networks, and other high-impact opportunities. Contribute to university-wide student success initiatives supporting new student transition and engagement, including Lawrence Launch, LUX events, EPIC experiences, Welcome Week, and other collaborative programs. Build strong partnerships with campus stakeholders to strengthen referral processes, reduce barriers to support, and create an integrated student success experience. Student Success Systems and Assessment Utilize the University’s Student Success Management System, Navigate360, to schedule appointments, document coaching interactions, coordinate interventions, manage caseloads, coordinate interventions, monitor student progress, and communicate with campus partners. Use coaching data, student outcomes, and assessment results to evaluate coaching effectiveness, identify emerging student needs, and contribute to the continuous improvement of student success initiatives. Contribute to a culture of continuous improvement by piloting new coaching approaches, programs, and initiatives that advance Lawrence University’s evolving vision for holistic student success. Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrated coaching, facilitation, and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to build trusting, developmental relationships that promote student learning, growth, and self-authorship. Knowledge of evidence-based learning strategies, metacognition, and academic success practices. Working knowledge of the Stanford Life Design framework, key themes from Hacking College , and related developmental coaching approaches (e.g., appreciative advising), or a demonstrated commitment to learning and applying these approaches to support students’ academic, personal, and career development. Ability to facilitate reflective, strengths-based, and action-oriented coaching conversations that help students connect their academic experiences, work, co-curricular and extracurricular involvement, personal values, and future aspirations. Commitment to meeting students where they are by listening actively, demonstrating empathy, and centering the student experience. Familiarity with career readiness frameworks (e.g., NACE Career Readiness Competencies) and the ability to help students connect their interests, strengths, experiences, and transferable skills to meaningful career pathways and post-graduate opportunities. Experience and demonstrated commitment to culturally responsive practice and working effectively with diverse student populations, including but not limited to first-generation students, international students, students with disabilities, LGBTQIA+ students, AAPI and BIPOC students, and students from a variety of cultural, religious, and socioeconomic backgrounds. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, academic advisors, and campus partners to provide coordinated, student-centered support, facilitate referrals, and advance student success. Demonstrated professionalism, sound judgment, and the ability to maintain confidentiality. Ability to manage multiple priorities, exercise initiative, and adapt effectively within a collaborative, evolving, and innovative student success environment. Familiarity with, or the ability to quickly learn, student success technologies including Navigate360, Microsoft Outlook, Microsoft Teams, Zoom, Banner, Canvas, and related platforms used to coordinate student support and assess outcomes. Appreciation for the value of a liberal arts education and Lawrence University’s commitment to intellectual curiosity, creativity, exploration, and holistic student development. Education and Work Experience Required Qualifications Completed Master’s degree in Higher Education, Counseling, Student Affairs, Educational Psychology, Social Work, College Student Personnel, or a similar field. Demonstrated experience coaching, advising, teaching, counseling, mentoring, or otherwise supporting college students in achieving academic, personal, or professional goals. Preferred Qualifications Three to five years of experience in higher education, preferably in academic coaching, advising, student success, counseling, or related direct student support roles. Certification in Academic Coaching, Life Design Coaching, or a related coaching program. Experience applying life design, design thinking, career development, student development, or strengths-based development frameworks with college students. University-level teaching experience. Significant experience working one-on-one with college students in a developmental or coaching capacity. Demonstrated commitment to equity, inclusion, and belonging. Experience with Navigate360 student success software. Experience with career coaching, career services, or career readiness programming. Application Materials Please submit: Cover Letter Resume A statement describing your philosophy of student success, advising, and coaching. We’re particularly interested in how you support students in identifying goals, leveraging their strengths, building meaningful connections, and designing purposeful academic and personal pathways. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S640P Number of Vacancies 2 Posting Date Best Consideration Date Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions Summary Anticipated Number of Hours per Week 40 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other If other, please specify (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Return To Lawrence Lawrence University 711 East Boldt Way Appleton, WI 54911 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com/postings/2164": {
      "title": "Lawrence University Portal | Assistant Director of Advancement Communications",
      "description": "Lawrence University Portal | Assistant Director of Advancement Communications Skip to Main Content Lawrence Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Director of Advancement Communications Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Director of Advancement Communications Location Appleton Department Alumni & Constituency Engagement Position Type Staff Position Description & Qualifications REPORTS TO: Director of Advancement Communications ABOUT US: The Advancement Team connects alumni and friends with Lawrence University’s mission by · Investing in relationships, · Matching donor and volunteer passions with university priorities, and · Demonstrating the impact of philanthropy and volunteer engagement on our students and their Lawrence experience PRIMARY OBJECTIVE : As the Assistant Director of Advancement Communications you will be responsible for the execution of a multi-channel marketing and communications plan that contributes to the University’s alumni and donor engagement goals. Your work will capture and share the Lawrence story in engaging and broad-reaching ways. This role will support fundraising priorities to support current and future students, steward donors, and engage our 20,000+ alumni – all while contributing to the university’s visibility and reputation as a leading liberal arts institution. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES : Support the Advancement division’s integrated marketing and communications efforts by contributing to alumni and donor engagement through compelling storytelling across multiple channels. Execute email campaigns designed to drive annual fund support, event registration, and alumni affinity and connectedness. Manage and grow our social media presence and engagement across the Lawrence University Alumni Facebook page, LinkedIn group, and Instagram page — including developing a strategic social media content calendar and designing visually compelling posts using Canva. Support digital storytelling strategies with print mail campaigns, coordinating print projects through external vendors. Serve as a primary resource with AlumnIQ, our email marketing platform, as well as ThankView, our donor stewardship email and video platform. Serve as a campus consultant, training other platform users to increase platform and channel effectiveness. Stay updated on best practices. Collaborate in design, content, and managing distribution of emails. Ensure emails align with best practices for optimal performance and accessibility. Provide quality assurance of email marketing efforts to ensure best practices and engagement tracking for communications across the division. Serve as a content contributor and coordinator for the alumni website. Assist in the creation and updating of microsites, special event sites, and other web products. Assist with writing, content generation, and editing expertise for the Advancement division. Support crowdfund initiatives with marketing and communications plans. Maintain the Advancement division email and event calendar, ensuring open and collaborative communication and planning amongst the various stakeholders. Maintain and respond to communications in the Alumni inbox with exemplary customer service and representing the University in a professional and compassionate manner. Support Advancement and University events as requested or required. Respond to special projects and other duties as assigned. Some evening and weekend work is required. WORKING RELATIONSHIPS : The Assistant Director will work most closely with the Advancement Team, particularly the Alumni and Community Engagement team. Additionally, the Assistant Director will work with faculty, students, and staff across campus and the University’s constituents—alumni, donors, parents, friends, and Fox Valley community members. The Assistant Director must establish and maintain positive working relationships with other key campus offices, such as Athletics, University Communications and Student Life, as well as off campus vendors for print solicitations and email marketing efforts. KNOWLEDGE AND SKILLS : Bachelor’s degree in related area with an appreciation for private, liberal arts, residential colleges. Two or more years relevant experience. Exceptional writing, communication, and editing skills, as well as accuracy and attention to detail. The ideal candidate will bring both copywriting and graphic design skills with the ability to create polished, on-brand digital content for social media and email. Familiarity with at least one major email marketing system. Demonstrated experience formatting letters, designing webpages, and managing social media platforms – Facebook, LinkedIn, and Instagram at a minimum. Solution oriented with a demonstrated ability to problem-solve. Demonstrated success in a fast-moving, multi-stakeholder environment, balancing multiple projects and priorities. Collaborative team player with a proactive attitude. Creativity, willingness to learn, and a sense of humor. Possess exceptional interpersonal and customer service skills i.e., concise, articulate, and confident with the ability to represent the university in a professional manner. Ability to maintain confidentiality of all aspects of job responsibilities. EMPLOYMENT REQUIREMENTS : Must have successful completion of criminal record check, driving record check (where applicable) and reference checks. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S638P Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Date Best Consideration Date Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions Summary Anticipated Number of Hours per Week 40 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other If other, please specify (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Return To Lawrence Lawrence University 711 East Boldt Way Appleton, WI 54911 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://lawrence.peopleadmin.com/postings/2170": {
      "title": "Lawrence Careers",
      "description": "Lawrence University Portal | Lead Carpenter Skip to Main Content Lawrence Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lead Carpenter Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Lead Carpenter Location Appleton Department Facility Operations Position Type Staff Position Description & Qualifications REPORTS TO: Assistant Director of Facilities Trades, Occupational and Environmental Safety LOCATION : Facilities Operations with daily assignments in university buildings throughout campus. HOURS OF WORK : 7:00am to 3:30 pm with occasional call ins DAYS OF WORK : Monday through Friday PRIMARY OBJECTIVE : Serve as lead carpenter, taking a leadership role on campus projects and assignments. Work independently and with other trades personnel to complete work orders related to carpentry and general maintenance in all university-owned buildings. Perform a variety of duties necessary to construct, install, and/or repair both the external and internal structure and fixtures of all types of university buildings. DUTIES : Construct, install, and repair partitions, cabinets, shelves, windows, screens and storms, and ironwork. Remodel basic frame structures. Install and repair suspended ceilings, formica, doors, door locks and checks, window balances, and various fixtures including drapery rods, shades and blinds, bathroom fixtures, toilet partitions, mirrors, bulletin boards, etc. Repair floors, plaster and dry wall, ceilings, furniture, etc. Paint and touch up walls as needed. Assist with training and supervision of student workers. Coordinate work orders. Additional tasks and assignments to assist in the overall mission of Facilities Operations. Oversee work being done by outside contractors. Timely completion and tracking of assigned work orders. Provide a high level of customer service and satisfaction by responding promptly to all customer requests and or complaints and communicate them to supervisor in a timely manner. MISCELLANEOUS DUTIES Engrave name plates. Repair garage doors. Install building and door signage throughout campus. Help with moving all types of furniture on campus. Oversee work being done by outside contractors. Additional tasks and assignments to assist in the overall mission of Facilities Operations. Act as a liaison between the facilities team, contractors, and vendors. WORKING RELATIONSHIPS : Will work collaboratively with all members of the Facilities Operations staff and occupants of the various university buildings where work is being performed. Must be able to provide excellent customer service to all members of the campus community, to respond to and work with students, faculty, and staff in a professional and courteous manner, and to work independently and with team members. KNOWLEDGE AND SKILLS REQUIRED : Ability to lead a small crew on various projects. Prefer 5-7 years previous carpentry experience. Must be able to lift 50 pounds. Must be able to climb using step and extension ladders. Helpful to have general knowledge of construction of garages, buildings, etc. Efficient and effective communication with supervisor, other tradesmen, and customers. Must possess excellent customer services skills. Self-starter who can complete assigned projects without supervision. Ability to read and follow oral or written instructions. General math skills. Basic computer skills and the ability to learn and use a computer including e-mail and online work orders or instructions. Excellent work attendance. Must be available for occasional after hours, weekend, on-call, and call-in duties. Ability to operate powered hand tools. EQUIPMENT USED : University vehicle. Trade related hand tools, common maintenance tools. Employment Requirements: Must have successful completion of criminal record check, pre-employment physical and pre-work screen, driving record check and reference checks. Must have a valid Driver’s License and must be able to pass the requirements to be a Lawrence University Driver and must complete campus drivers training. Must have a minimum of a high school diploma or equivalent. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S620P Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Date Best Consideration Date Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions Summary Anticipated Number of Hours per Week 40 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other If other, please specify (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter Return To Lawrence Lawrence University 711 East Boldt Way Appleton, WI 54911 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
